    [Doc] Clarify DSpark adaptive verification restrictions (#19387)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Add a warning to the English speculative decoding guide for DSpark
    adaptive verification with a confidence head. State the Model Runner V2
    requirement and clarify that fully eager execution and pure `PIECEWISE`
    graph mode are unsupported for the target model when this feature is
    enabled, in both vLLM Ascend and vLLM. Document the PP, PCP, DCP, LM
    head TP, LoRA, and commercial-use restrictions in vLLM Ascend. Set
    `FULL_DECODE_ONLY` explicitly in the adaptive verification example.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation clarification only; runtime behavior is unchanged.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Inspected the adaptive verification configuration checks in vLLM
    `v0.30.0` and `main` to confirm the execution-mode restriction applies
    when `enable_adaptive_verification` is enabled.
    - Checked the amendment diff and added whitespace; all code examples
    remain unchanged by this wording update. Python and Shell example syntax
    was validated previously.
    - Verified that the PR contains one commit and changes only the English
    Markdown guide; no `.po` changes are included.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci`; it could not run because `pre-commit`
    is unavailable locally. Formatting and documentation build validation
    remain for CI.
    - No runtime tests were added or run for this documentation-only change.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
